    "AGY and environment JSON key names are not pinned. source-matrix status is planned_contract_no_schema_fixture_yet. T09 owns the AGY reader. This oracle pins only their numeric limits and the no-vendor-format claim.",
    "No admitted adapter states a numeric carryover byte budget. The pinned carryover rule is the existing one: a trailing partial without LF is absent from the batch and from the prefix hash, and the watermark stays at its first byte.",
    "An undelimited record longer than max+1 is not required to be scanned until a later LF. The required result is the existing export error with an unmoved watermark, or a quarantine that retains no bytes and does not claim EOF.",
    "Creating a Windows symlink can fail for lack of privilege. When a symlink is actually presented, the refusal string is required. Inability to create the fixture is not_attempted, not a pass.",
    "file_path in the watermark is the SHA-256 of the canonical OsStr encoded bytes, so its hex value is machine-dependent and is not an expected constant. session_id hashes above are hashes of consumed file bytes only.",
    "last_modified is filesystem mtime and is not an expected constant.",
    "Depth counting and the 1024*1024-byte MiB are fixed by T05 lead contract clarification. LF and CRLF framing bytes are included in encoded limits; other formats must declare framing. The original Grok draft predates that clarification.",
    "duplicate_json_key is an oracle-assigned code. Current serde_json::Value decoding is last-wins and is not the expected result. DESIGN requires duplicate-key handling and does not name this string.",
    "Collector 64/600/1s limits are DESIGN bounds. source-matrix still says native_feasibility_and_synthetic_execution_pending. Registering the equal bound does not admit a producer specimen.",
    "B01-G admits only the exact two sanitized fixture digests in its current profile, with native parser T08 still pending. Linux strace and Windows ETW remain blocked pending real profiles and controlled specimens. This draft claims no version-wide Grok admission or trace grammar."
